Report Add-On: Frontend Implementation (Next.js Interface)
Frontend Overview

A lightweight frontend was developed using Next.js to demonstrate the usability and real-time interaction of the SmartEdU IR system. Although the coursework primarily focuses on backend IR design and evaluation, the UI supports practical testing, better illustrating system performance, highlighting, and snippet features.

The interface allows users to:

Enter search queries

View structured and unstructured retrieval results

Observe keyword highlighting and contextual snippets

Select retrieval mode (exact / fuzzy / hybrid)

Inspect system response time for each query

This aligns with IR usability principles recommending accessible interfaces for query input and ranked results presentation (Manning, Raghavan & Schütze, 2008).

UI Flow

User enters a query into the search bar

Next.js calls the backend using fetch("/api/search?q=<term>")

Results are grouped into Students, Courses, and Documents

<mark> tags from the backend are rendered in the UI to highlight matched terms

Response time is displayed for performance transparency

Key Frontend Components
Component	Description
Search input	Accepts query string and triggers backend call
Query mode switcher	Allows user selection: exact / fuzzy / hybrid
Results renderer	Groups and lists students, courses, documents
HTML-safe highlight rendering	Displays highlighted terms securely
Snippet display	Shows contextual previews for documents
Performance display	Shows response time and record count
Rendering Highlights Safely

To preserve <mark> tags returned from the backend while preventing HTML injection, the UI uses a controlled HTML rendering function (e.g. dangerouslySetInnerHTML with sanitisation).

This approach follows secure rendering practices recommended in IR systems that generate HTML-formatted results (Büttcher, Clarke & Cormack, 2016).

